# Google Drive import. Leave these unset and the "Upload from Google Drive"
# option is hidden - device upload keeps working.
#
# Google Cloud console > APIs & Services:
#   1. Enable "Google Drive API" and "Google Picker API".
#   2. Credentials > API key       -> VITE_GOOGLE_API_KEY
#      Restrict it to the Picker API and to your site's origins.
#   3. Credentials > OAuth client ID, type "Web application" -> VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID
#      Authorised JavaScript origins must list every origin you serve from,
#      e.g. https://your-app.up.railway.app and http://localhost:5173.
#      Google rejects LAN addresses (http://192.168.x.x) as origins.
#
# These are inlined at build time - rebuild after changing them.
#   4. The project number from the console dashboard -> VITE_GOOGLE_APP_ID
#      Required, not optional. With the drive.file scope the picker only grants
#      the app access to the picked file if it is built with the project number,
#      so without this the picker works and the download then fails with 404.

VITE_GOOGLE_API_KEY=
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
VITE_GOOGLE_APP_ID=
